tools.example:
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").set("SolidModel", "Orthotropic");
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").set("coordinateSystem", "sys2");
model.component("comp1").material("mat1").propertyGroup().create("Orthotropic", "Orthotropic");
model.component("comp1").material("mat1").propertyGroup("Orthotropic").set("Evector", new String[]{"140[GPa]", "10[GPa]", "10[GPa]"});
model.component("comp1").material("mat1").propertyGroup("Orthotropic").set("nuvector", new String[]{"0.3", "0.4", "0.3"});
model.component("comp1").material("mat1").propertyGroup("Orthotropic").set("Gvector", new String[]{"5[GPa]", "3.6[GPa]", "5[GPa]"});

model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").set("SolidModel", "Anisotropic");
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").set("AnisotropicOption", "AnisotropicVo");
// fill the DVo group of the material with homogenized stiffness values from a Cell Periodicity study

model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("hmm1").set("MaterialModel", "Ogden");
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("hmm1").set("Compressibility_Ogden", "NearlyIncompressible");
// GUI: Ogden parameters table, e.g. (0.63 MPa, 1.3), (0.0012 MPa, 5.0), (-0.01 MPa, -2.0)

Solid Mechanics > Hyperelastic Material 1 > Material model: Fung, Coordinate system: Curvilinear System (cc)
Compressibility: Compressible
// Application Library: Nonlinear_Structural_Materials_Module/Hyperelasticity/arterial_wall_mechanics

Model Wizard > Structural Mechanics > Electromagnetics-Structure Interaction > Magnetostriction > Piezomagnetism
Solid Mechanics > Piezomagnetic Material 1: Stress-magnetization form, material Terfenol-D (linearized)
// Application Library: Structural_Mechanics_Module/Magnetomechanics/piezomagnetic_cell_rover

model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").create("sf1", "Safety", 3);
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").feature("sf1").set("FailureCriterion", "Von Mises");
model.component("comp1").physics("solid").feature("lemm1").feature("sf1").set("sigmat", "350[MPa]");
// then Study > Update Solution and plot the safety factor
